"""Reproduce the manually reviewed evidence ledger; no web scraping or financial execution."""
import json
from pathlib import Path

sources = []
def source(id, title, authority, url, locator, evidence, limitation='', published=''):
    sources.append(dict(id=id,title=title,authority=authority,url=url,locator=locator,evidence=evidence,limitation=limitation,published=published,accessed='2026-11-07',method='Official page body retrieved and read with fetch_page'))
source('S01','Administrative Rules on Individual’s Foreign Exchange','PBOC','https://www.pbc.gov.cn/english/130733/2025080815071447034/index.html','Articles 2–9, 13–15, 20','Article 13 allows non-domestic individuals to convert legitimate RMB current-account income and remit abroad with identity and relevant documents. Article 7 prohibits splitting to evade limits and fabricated vouchers.','Old promulgation date; cross-checked against the 2026 SAFE FAQ. English chapter-three heading appears mistranslated as current account.','2006-12-25 (page dated 2007-01-31)')
source('S02','Individual FX implementing rules, amended republication','SAFE Tianjin','https://www.safe.gov.cn/tianjin/2024/0430/2464.html','Articles 2–4, 13–15, 20–21, 28, 38; amendment notes','Article 2: 对个人结汇和境内个人购汇实行年度总额管理。年度总额分别为每人每年等值5万美元。 Article 13 requires identity and income-source documents including tax vouchers for an overseas individual’s lawful RMB income. Article 15 distinguishes account FX from cash.','Article 39 is reproduced but explicitly repealed in the footnote; do not use its penalty amounts. Translations on this site are working summaries, not certified translations.','2024-04-30 republication')
source('S03','2026 personal FX FAQ: employment remuneration','SAFE Tianjin','https://www.safe.gov.cn/tianjin/2026/0713/3088.html','Answer quoting Article 59 of the 2020 current-account guidelines','境外个人在境内取得的经常项目合法人民币收入，凭本人有效身份证件和有交易额的购汇资金来源材料（含税务凭证）在银行办理购汇。','Confirms documentary route; does not quote a universal numeric salary cap or guarantee a specific bank’s acceptance.','2026-07-13')
source('S04','Individual Foreign Exchange Services Guide for Non-Chinese Mainland Individuals','HSBC China (bank primary source)','https://www.hsbc.com.cn/content/dam/hsbc/cn/docs/foreign-exchange/personal-foreign-exchange-business-handling-guide-en.pdf','Sections: FX purchase; property transfers; property transactions; outbound remittances','Employment income: employment/service contract or certificate, employer income statement and tax payment certificate. Property-sale remittance cannot exceed net proceeds after taxes and fees; ownership transfer must be registered. Immigration/inherited property transfers require SAFE approval documents.','Bank policy, not a regulator. Its opening quota wording differs from S02; flagged F02. Publication/effective date not established. PDF retrieved chunks 0–1.','')
source('S05','Guide to CNY transfers','Wise (provider primary source)','https://wise.com/help/articles/2955298/guide-to-cny-transfers','Sending FROM CNY (not the inbound sections)','Eligible: not mainland Chinese, working or previously worked in China, tax record showing taxes paid within the last 3 years. Own-account destinations only. Bank-app single-transfer maximum 300,000 CNY; Alipay maximum 50,000 CNY. Overall limit generally after-tax salary; Skyremit transfers affect remaining limit.','Provider-specific eligibility, not a universal legal limit. Generic marketing pages are not relied upon for payment methods or recipients. No live fee quote obtained.','')
source('S06','Transfers and Remittance','HSBC China (bank primary source)','https://www.hsbc.com.cn/en-cn/transfer-payments/','International transfers / Global Transfer','Global Transfer to Self supports cross-border foreign-currency transfers to own overseas HSBC accounts; listed currencies include USD. Free for eligible Premier, Premier Elite and Global Private Banking customers.','Free transfer service does not establish a free FX spread, third-party fees or personal eligibility. Scope read: chunk 0.','')
source('S07','Wealth and Personal Banking tariff','HSBC China (bank primary source)','https://www.hsbc.com.cn/content/dam/hsbc/cn/docs/document-download/tariff-of-Accounts-services-for-personal-customers-v2.pdf','Important notes 1, 3, 7; item 2.2.4.1 (Premier column)','Effective from 31 Oct 2026. Premier telegraphic-transfer issuance: 0.1% of remittance amount, minimum CNY100, maximum CNY500, plus cable charge. Charges exclude other institutions’ charges and government duties/taxes.','Only the Premier issuance column is used here, not a universal bank price. Total cable, spread and receiver costs not established. Read chunks 0, 5–7.','Effective 2026-10-31')
source('S08','Regulating large-sum overseas cash withdrawals: Q&A','SAFE','https://www.safe.gov.cn/en/2017/1230/1391.html','Answers 2, 3, 5, 6','Aggregate overseas withdrawals across domestic cards: RMB100,000 per person per calendar year; daily per-card quota RMB10,000. Lending/borrowing cards to evade controls prohibited. Normal overseas consumption does not offset annual FX-purchase quota.','Old policy publication; issuing-bank and ATM restrictions may be tighter. Not a channel for disguising capital transfer as consumption.','2017-12-30; effective 2018-01-01')
source('S09','Foreign-currency cash entry/exit measures','SAFE / General Administration of Customs','https://www.safe.gov.cn/tianjin/2024/0430/2466.html','Cover notice, paragraph 2','Ordinary outbound foreign-currency cash up to USD5,000 equivalent needs no carrying permit; over USD5,000 through USD10,000 needs a bank permit. Above USD10,000 is generally prohibited except special circumstances with SAFE permit.','Cover notice read. Prior inward declarations and repeated crossings require separate analysis; not a blanket rule for every traveler.','2024-04-30 republication of 2003 notice')
source('S10','Individual Income Tax Law (2018 amendment)','Guangzhou Finance Bureau (official government republication)','https://czj.gz.gov.cn/zwgk/zfxxgkml/czyjs/jsjfxx/content/post_4466375.html','Articles 1–6, 8, 10–15, 18; rate schedules','Comprehensive income progressive rates 3%–45%; business income 5%–35%; listed interest/dividend/rent/asset-transfer/incidental income statutory rate 20%. Asset-transfer taxable base is income minus original value and reasonable expenses.','Statutory framework, not an individualized effective rate. Exemptions, treaty, implementing rules and local property taxes not resolved. Article 18 separately governs savings-deposit interest changes.','2019-06-14 republication')
source('S11','U.S. citizens and resident aliens abroad','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/us-citizens-and-resident-aliens-abroad','Opening paragraphs; foreign financial accounts / Form 3520','U.S. citizens are subject to tax on worldwide income; benefits require relevant returns. Foreign-account reporting may apply even if no taxable income is generated.','Does not calculate personal tax or establish state-tax treatment.','')
source('S12','Foreign Tax Credit','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/foreign-tax-credit','Qualifying foreign taxes / compliance issues','Qualifying foreign income taxes may be credited or deducted; credit generally claimed on Form 1116. Taxes on income excluded under FEIE cannot also generate a foreign tax credit. Treaty-reduced tax, not excess withholding, may be the creditable amount.','Eligibility, source, category and limits require individual analysis; fees and spread are not automatically creditable income taxes.','')
source('S13','Foreign earned income exclusion','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/foreign-earned-income-exclusion','Qualification requirements / other rules','Foreign earned income, foreign tax home and bona fide residence or qualifying physical presence required. U.S. citizen physical-presence alternative: 330 full days during 12 consecutive months.','Not a bank-transfer exemption; no current annual exclusion amount used because retrieved overview lists older years.','')
source('S14','Report of Foreign Bank and Financial Accounts','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/report-of-foreign-bank-and-financial-accounts-fbar','Who must file; when to file; keeping records; penalties','U.S. person with reportable interest/authority must file if aggregate foreign accounts exceed USD10,000 at any time in calendar year. April 15 due date with automatic October 15 extension. Generally keep records five years. Civil penalty maxima adjusted annually.','No 2026 inflation-adjusted penalty figure verified; current numeric maximum intentionally blank.','')
source('S15','Comparison of Form 8938 and FBAR requirements','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/businesses/comparison-of-form-8938-and-fbar-requirements','Reporting threshold and penalties rows','8938: U.S.-living unmarried/separate filers over USD50,000 year-end or USD75,000 any time; joint over USD100,000/150,000. Abroad unmarried/separate over USD200,000/300,000; joint over USD400,000/600,000. Form 8938 does not replace FBAR.','Abroad classification is a statutory test, not browser location. Historical FBAR penalty figures on this page must not be treated as current.','')
source('S16','Gifts from foreign person','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/businesses/gifts-from-foreign-person','General rule / reporting requirements / covered expatriates','Foreign individual/estate gifts or bequests over USD100,000 aggregated with related parties require reporting; corporate/partnership purported gifts have a different threshold. Covered-expatriate gifts can have separate tax consequences.','Genuine gifts only. Own-account transfers are not gifts from another person; foreign trusts require separate treatment.','')
source('S17','Foreign currency and currency exchange rates','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/foreign-currency-and-currency-exchange-rates','Functional currency / exchange rates','Report U.S. return amounts in USD; dollar-functional taxpayers translate relevant income/expenses/taxes at applicable receipt/payment/accrual exchange rates.','A current bank quote is not a historical tax-basis rate; no live CNY/USD quote verified.','')
source('S18','26 USC 988, 2024 edition','U.S. Government Publishing Office','https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2024-title26/html/USCODE-2024-title26-subtitleA-chap1-subchapN-partIII-subpartJ-sec988.htm','Subsections (a), (c)(1)(C), (e)','General section-988 treatment is ordinary income/loss; nonfunctional currency includes bank demand/time deposits. Subsection (e) contains a narrow personal-currency-disposition exception for gains not exceeding USD200.','2024 edition only; later amendment status not independently established. The USD200 rule is not a blanket annual deduction and personal applicability is unverified.','2024 edition')
source('S19','Streamlined filing compliance procedures','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/streamlined-filing-compliance-procedures','Eligibility; voluntary disclosure vs streamlined','Non-willfulness certification required; existing civil examination or criminal investigation precludes streamlined eligibility. Those concerned about willfulness should consult legal/professional advisers.','No personal certification or eligibility conclusion made.','')
source('S20','Streamlined Foreign Offshore Procedures','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/us-taxpayers-residing-outside-the-united-states','Eligibility; scope and effect','Qualifying non-willful taxpayers submit three covered years of returns and six covered years of FBARs and pay tax/interest; specified penalties not imposed when requirements met. Citizen nonresidency test includes no U.S. abode and 330 full days abroad in a covered year.','Current physical location does not establish eligibility. Previously assessed penalties not abated by this procedure.','')
source('S21','Streamlined Domestic Offshore Procedures','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/us-taxpayers-residing-in-the-united-states','Eligibility; scope and effect','Qualifying domestic procedure includes three years amended returns, six years FBARs, tax/interest and a 5% miscellaneous offshore penalty on the defined highest aggregate covered asset balance/value.','Not a 5% conversion fee or automatic choice for every domestic taxpayer; prior returns and non-willfulness requirements apply.','')
source('S22','Money and Other Monetary Instruments','U.S. Customs and Border Protection','https://www.cbp.gov/travel/international-visitors/money-monetary-instruments','Who must file; what is a monetary instrument','More than USD10,000 currency/monetary instruments at one time crossing U.S. border requires reporting. Families/groups aggregate; electronic FinCEN 105 available.','Applies to physical transportation/mail/shipment, not a universal USD10,000 wire tax.','Last modified 2025-11-24')
source('S23','Virtual currency and tokenization risk notice, Yinfa [2026] 42','PBOC and seven other authorities','https://www.pbc.gov.cn/tiaofasi/144941/3581332/2026020619591971323/index.html','Sections I(1), III(6), legal liability and final paragraph','Domestic fiat/virtual-currency exchange and related business activities strictly prohibited; financial/payment institutions cannot provide account opening, transfers or settlement for virtual-currency business. Notice repeals Yinfa [2021] 237.','Working English summary of Chinese text; no claim that every act of merely holding cryptocurrency is criminal.','2026-02-06')
source('S24','China – Tax treaty documents','IRS','https://www.irs.gov/businesses/international-businesses/china-tax-treaty-documents','Treaty and technical explanation links','IRS provides the 1984 income-tax treaty and technical explanation.','Index verified only. No treaty article, reduced rate or savings-clause exception applied without substantive treaty review.','')

rows=[]
def row(id, category, topic, finding, sources, locator, status='Source-backed', value='', pros='', cons=''):
    rows.append(dict(id=id,category=category,topic=topic,finding=finding,sources=sources.split(),locator=locator,status=status,value=value,pros=pros,cons=cons))
# Legal bases and delivery channels are distinct; these are NOT cumulative quotas.
row('R01','routes','Documented salary → bank USD wire','Primary route to investigate for a foreign individual’s lawful China employment income. Present identity and amount-specific income-source/tax records; convert through an authorized bank, then remit. The regulator does not state a universal numeric salary cap in this FAQ.','S03 S01 S04','SAFE 2026 answer; PBOC Art.13; HSBC employment income',pros='Direct official documentary route; avoids inventing a new sale or gift.',cons='Acceptance depends on source trail, tax records and the bank’s classification. Fees/spread remain.')
row('R02','routes','Other lawful current-account income → bank','Use the lawful-income documentary route where the money is not salary. HSBC requires proof of source and supporting tax-payment certificates for other lawful current-account income. Do not relabel capital proceeds as salary.','S01 S04','PBOC Art.13; HSBC FX purchases',pros='May address lawful income other than wages.',cons='Category and tax treatment must be established; not an unrestricted route for every deposit.')
row('R03','routes','Pension, severance or compensation → bank','HSBC’s guide lists source documents from the disbursing organization for pensions, severance, retirement benefits and compensation. This is a documented category, not confirmation that this account contains qualifying funds.','S04','FX purchases: lawfully earned RMB',pros='Specific bank documentary category.',cons='Chinese and U.S. taxation and any pension/trust reporting require separate review.')
row('R04','routes','Wise: bank-app-funded CNY → own USD account','Provider route for eligible non-mainland individuals who work/worked in China and have accepted tax records showing taxes paid within the last 3 years. Transfers must go to another account they own; overall limit generally tied to after-tax salary.','S05','Sending from CNY: eligibility, recipients, limits',value='300,000 CNY per transfer via bank app',pros='Digital channel; own overseas bank or Wise-account destination.',cons='Provider verification and salary-based limit; not established for arbitrary savings, gifts or property proceeds. Exact fee unverified.')
row('R05','routes','Wise: Alipay-funded CNY → own account','Alternative funding channel within the same Wise from-CNY service, not a second independent allowance. Same own-account and tax-record eligibility requirements.','S05','Sending from CNY: Alipay; total sending limits',value='50,000 CNY per transfer via Alipay',pros='Alternative app funding method.',cons='Lower per-transfer ceiling; do not confuse with Wise’s inbound-to-China Alipay product.')
row('R06','routes','HSBC Global Transfer after lawful FX purchase','Delivery channel for eligible customers with overseas HSBC accounts. The service transfers foreign currency, including USD; RMB conversion/document review must still be satisfied first.','S06 S03','Global Transfer to Self; SAFE documentary route',pros='Advertised free Global Transfer for eligible Premier/Elite/Private Banking customers.',cons='Not a capital-control exemption. FX spread, account eligibility and any other costs are not established as free.')
row('R07','routes','Remit an existing foreign-currency balance','If the funds are already USD or another foreign currency in an overseas individual’s Chinese FX savings account, the implementing rules allow outward current-account remittance with valid identity. This differs from converting a CNY balance.','S02 S04','SAFE Art.15(1); HSBC outbound remittances',pros='Can avoid an unnecessary CNY→USD conversion if already USD.',cons='Does not help a wholly CNY balance; bank due diligence and source classification remain.')
row('R08','routes','Return unused imported foreign exchange','PBOC Article 14 allows a non-domestic individual to return unused foreign exchange remitted from abroad through the original route with identity documents.','S01','Article 14',pros='Original-route return specifically recognized.',cons='Only unused imported FX; do not assume it covers domestic RMB earnings or every RMB conversion of imported capital.')
row('R09','routes','Reconvert leftover RMB from prior travel exchange','Unused RMB from a qualifying earlier exchange can be reconverted with identity and original exchange slip. Small-amount exceptions exist; the exchange-slip rule is not a general undocumented salary quota.','S02 S04','SAFE Art.13(2); HSBC unused-RMB reconversion',value='Slip valid 24 months; ID-only ≤USD500/day, or ≤USD1,000/day at specified departure locations',pros='Recognized return route for qualifying leftover exchanged money.',cons='Original-source and amount restrictions; not a scalable shortcut for unexplained savings.')
row('R10','routes','Foreign-owner property-sale net proceeds','HSBC lists identity, transfer contract, ownership registration and relevant tax evidence/filing. Ownership transfer must be registered; remittance limited to net sale proceeds after taxes/fees and the owner’s share.','S04 S02','HSBC property-sale proceeds; SAFE Art.21',pros='Capital-specific route rather than misusing a travel quota.',cons='Property-sale tax obligations remain. Pre-immigration/inherited assets may need a different route; no local effective tax rate confirmed.')
row('R11','routes','Refund from unsuccessful property purchase','HSBC lists original FX settlement receipt, contract termination, housing-authority cancellation and identity; a representative requires notarized power of attorney.','S04','Property transactions: refunded payments',pros='Recognized refund category.',cons='Only genuine failed purchases; not a reason to create a sham purchase or cancellation.')
row('R12','routes','Inherited mainland property → approved transfer','Implementing rules place foreign citizens’ lawful mainland inheritance transfers under the personal-property-transfer regime. HSBC requires a SAFE approval document from the deceased’s former-domicile jurisdiction.','S02 S04','SAFE Art.20; HSBC inherited property transfers',pros='Dedicated inheritance framework.',cons='Approval and inheritance evidence required; USD100,000 U.S. gift/bequest reporting test is separate from Chinese transfer permission.')
row('R13','routes','Pre-immigration property → approved transfer','The implementing rules cover domestic individuals’ lawful property acquired before legal immigration status. HSBC lists identity and SAFE approval from the former domicile. This is not automatic merely because the owner is now a U.S. citizen.','S02 S04','SAFE Art.20; HSBC immigration-related transfers',pros='Potentially relevant for assets predating emigration.',cons='Former status, acquisition dates and approvals unverified; not a general expat-savings entitlement.')
row('R14','routes','Authorized representative at bank','An execution arrangement, not a separate tax or quota route. SAFE permits agency handling with required identity, authorization and transaction evidence; HSBC specifies notarized power of attorney for property transactions.','S02 S04','SAFE Arts.4, 38; HSBC property sections',pros='May reduce need to travel personally for supported transactions.',cons='Remote acceptance and exact notarization/legalization rules for this bank are unverified. Required client authorization cannot be automated away.')
row('R15','routes','Overseas ATM withdrawals','Domestic-card overseas withdrawals have aggregate yearly and per-card daily controls. Borrowing/lending cards to evade them is prohibited. USD availability and actual bank/ATM costs not verified.','S08','Answers 2–3',value='RMB100,000 per person/year; RMB10,000 per card/day',pros='Limited access to cash for genuine needs.',cons='Cash handling, issuer/ATM limits and unquoted costs; not the default for large savings or control avoidance.')
row('R16','routes','Genuine overseas card spending','Alternative to repatriation: SAFE describes normal overseas catering, accommodation, transport and shopping consumption; it does not offset the annual FX-purchase quota. This does not deposit USD into a U.S. bank account.','S08','Answer 3',pros='Can meet real expenses without first wiring USD.',cons='Not cash extraction or permission for fake merchant transactions; merchant acceptance and FX costs unverified.')
row('R17','routes','Lawfully purchased USD cash carried abroad','Physical transport only after lawful conversion/withdrawal. Ordinary outbound rules distinguish ≤USD5,000, bank-permitted >USD5,000 to USD10,000, and exceptional SAFE-permitted larger amounts. U.S. reporting independently applies.','S09 S22 S03','SAFE cover notice para.2; CBP who must file',pros='Recognized small-cash option.',cons='Theft, travel and declaration/permit risks; prior-declaration/repeated-crossing exceptions require review. No tax saving established.')
row('R18','routes','Domestic-individual current-account quota','Conditional comparator, not an assumed route for this U.S. citizen. SAFE Article 2 states USD50,000 annual management for individual settlement and domestic-individual purchase; above-quota genuine current-account purchase has documentation rules.','S02','Arts.2, 12, 14',value='USD50,000 equivalent annual amount in Art.2',pros='Simplified handling where the legal classification actually applies.',cons='Does not authorize unrestricted capital export; account classification cannot be inferred from citizenship alone or changed using another person’s identity.')
row('R19','routes','Hong Kong / offshore RMB then USD','A possible destination structure to assess, not a verified independent extraction route. No account-specific permission to send this mainland CNY offshore or cheaper two-leg quote was established.','S01 S02','Current/capital distinctions; approved channels',status='Unverified',pros='Potential offshore conversion comparison only after a lawful outbound route is confirmed.',cons='Opening a Hong Kong account does not itself prove mainland transfer permission. Two conversion/transfer legs may add cost.')
row('R20','routes','Corporate dividend, equity exit or genuine loan repayment','Not verified as a route for the described personal balance. Ownership, registered investment/debt, transaction documents and tax category are unknown; personal and business money must not be conflated.','S01 S10','PBOC current/capital classification; IIT Arts.2–3',status='Unverified',pros='Could require a separate corporate/capital-account study if source actually qualifies.',cons='No eligibility, corporate withholding rate, repayment exemption or exact paperwork confirmed. Not a manufactured workaround.')
row('R21','routes','Crypto / stablecoin bridge','Not recommended as a workaround. The 2026 multi-agency notice strictly prohibits domestic fiat/virtual-currency exchange business and bars financial/payment services for virtual-currency business.','S23','I(1), III(6), final paragraph',status='Do not use',pros='',cons='Regulatory and asset-loss risk; crypto does not erase tax/reporting obligations. Use current 2026 notice, not repealed 2021 notice.')
row('R22','routes','Friends’ quotas, underground swaps or fake invoices','Do not split transactions to evade controls or use fabricated transaction documents. PBOC explicitly prohibits quota evasion through splitting and false vouchers; no lawful underground-swap route was verified.','S01 S02','PBOC Arts.5, 7; SAFE authenticity review',status='Do not use',pros='',cons='Cannot compare an unverified evasion scheme as a legitimate tax-saving option. No evasion instructions provided.')
# Costs: applicable figures deliberately blank where not confirmed.
row('C01','costs','Chinese tax on the source of funds','The IIT law taxes specified income categories, not a named universal CNY→USD conversion percentage. Analysis: identify whether the quoted “tax” is unpaid source-income tax, asset-sale tax, fee or spread before evaluating it. This is not an individualized zero-tax determination.','S10 S03','IIT Arts.2–6; SAFE documentary requirements',status='Analysis',pros='Separate already-paid taxes from new liabilities.',cons='Exact personal tax amount unverified; payment proof may still be required.')
row('C02','costs','Bank FX spread','Compare the executable USD selling quote for buying USD with a same-time reference rate, in the same units. No executable rate or spread was confirmed for this account.','S06 S17','HSBC exchange-rate link; IRS currency guidance',status='Unverified',cons='Headline mid-market or historic reporting rates are not a guaranteed customer quote.')
row('C03','costs','HSBC Premier wire issuance example','Published tariff example only: issuance fee is 0.1% of remittance amount, min CNY100, max CNY500, plus cable charge. Do not apply the Premier column to an unidentified bank/account.','S07','Item 2.2.4.1 Premier column',value='0.1%; CNY100 minimum; CNY500 maximum; plus cable',cons='This is not the all-in transfer cost. Tier eligibility and other components remain unverified.')
row('C04','costs','Cable / SWIFT message fee','The HSBC example explicitly adds a cable charge, but this study did not establish the applicable numeric cable amount for this account.','S07','Item 2.2.4.1',status='Unverified',cons='Leave quote blank; do not silently fold into an estimated percentage.')
row('C05','costs','Intermediary and receiving-bank deductions','HSBC tariff notes exclude other institutions’ charges. Receiver and correspondent deductions for the user’s path have not been established.','S07','Important note 7',status='Unverified',cons='A bank’s fee waiver is not proof that the beneficiary receives the full gross amount.')
row('C06','costs','Wise fee / executable USD proceeds','Eligibility and limits are source-backed, but no personalized live CNY→USD quote was obtained. Website marketing examples are not used as a universal fee schedule.','S05','Sending from CNY; provider pricing link',status='Unverified',cons='Compare final USD credited for the same total CNY debited; do not assume Wise is cheapest.')
row('C07','costs','U.S. tax on FX gain','Section 988 distinguishes foreign-currency gain from transferred principal. Deposits are included in the statute’s nonfunctional-currency definition. Basis, acquisition dates and personal/investment classification must be established.','S18 S17','988(a), (c)(1)(C), (e); IRS functional currency',status='Needs review',cons='2024 statutory edition; later-amendment status and personal treatment not independently verified. No personal gain/tax estimate supplied.')
row('C08','costs','Compliance penalties / interest','These are consequences of prior filing/payment failures, not automatically a conversion surcharge. FBAR maxima change with inflation; exact current maximum was not verified.','S14 S19','FBAR penalties; streamlined eligibility',status='Needs review',cons='No safe-transfer size cures prior noncompliance. Avoid treating reporting thresholds as tax-free allowances.')
row('C09','costs','Documents, representation and travel','Source documents and authorization may be required. No official case-specific translation, notarization, adviser or travel prices were established.','S04 S02','HSBC property representation; SAFE Art.38',status='Unverified',cons='Compare process costs as well as bank fees; do not assume remote processing is available.')
row('C10','costs','Effective execution drag: analytical formula','Let A be total CNY debited, q the simultaneous reference CNY per USD, and N final USD credited. Benchmark USD = A/q. Execution drag = A/q − N; drag % = 100 × (1 − Nq/A). Derived comparison formula, not an official fee or tax rule.','S06 S07','Bank FX/rate and tariff inputs',status='Analysis',cons='Requires confirmed A, q and N. Source taxes and later U.S. taxes are separate; avoid double-counting fees already included in A or N.')
row('C11','costs','Net USD formula for a single conversion','If B CNY is the starting balance, T actual unpaid Chinese tax, Fc CNY costs deducted before conversion, r executable CNY per USD, and Fu USD costs deducted afterward: net USD = (B − T − Fc)/r − Fu. Derived accounting identity for this sequence only.','S03 S07 S10','Tax evidence; tariff; source tax framework',status='Analysis',cons='No placeholder numbers, no assumed tax rate. Adjust timing for fees debited separately; reserve any U.S. liability separately.')
row('C12','costs','Best-price conclusion','No route can be certified cheapest without verified source category and same-time, all-in executable quotes. Recommendation: assess documented bank remittance first; compare Wise for eligible salary funds and HSBC Global Transfer for eligible existing customers.','S03 S05 S06 S07','Route eligibility and pricing limitations',status='Analysis',cons='This ranking is a process recommendation, not a personalized eligibility finding or tax opinion.')
# US and Chinese tax/reference rows
row('T01','taxes','China comprehensive income','Statutory progressive range on taxable comprehensive income; it is not a flat percentage of the bank balance. Residency, deductions, source year and prior payments affect actual liability.','S10','Arts.1–3, 6; rate schedule',value='3%–45% marginal rates')
row('T02','taxes','China business income','Statutory progressive range applies to taxable business income, not automatically to moving personal savings.','S10','Arts.3, 6; second rate schedule',value='5%–35% marginal rates')
row('T03','taxes','China asset transfers and other listed categories','Law lists a 20% statutory rate for interest/dividends, rent, asset transfers and incidental income; exemptions/specific rules must be checked. Asset-transfer taxable base deducts original asset value and reasonable expenses; do not tax gross sale proceeds mechanically.','S10','Arts.3, 4, 6(5), 18',value='20% statutory rate; personal effective rate unverified')
row('T04','taxes','U.S. worldwide income','U.S. citizens generally report taxable income worldwide whether retained in China or remitted. Analysis: moving already-owned principal should not be confused with earning new income; source income, interest and currency gain must still be analyzed.','S11 S18','IRS opening paragraphs; 988',status='Analysis')
row('T05','taxes','Foreign tax credit','Eligible foreign income taxes may reduce U.S. income tax subject to rules and limits; Form 1116 is generally used for individuals. No credit for taxes on FEIE-excluded income. Bank charges are not automatically eligible income taxes.','S12','Qualifying taxes; how to claim; compliance issues',pros='Lawful way to address potential double taxation.',cons='Not an automatic full offset; categories, timing, source and treaty entitlement matter.')
row('T06','taxes','Foreign earned income exclusion','Requires qualifying foreign earned income, tax home and residence/presence test. Cannot assume eligibility based on U.S. citizenship, money held in China or current browser location. No current-year dollar cap applied.','S13','Qualification and other rules',pros='Potential relief for qualifying earnings.',cons='Not a conversion exemption; coordinate with FTC; does not simply shelter interest, asset gains or arbitrary savings.')
row('T07','taxes','FBAR','Report qualifying foreign accounts when aggregate value exceeds USD10,000 at any time in calendar year, even if no income. File separately with FinCEN; April 15 with automatic extension to October 15. Emptying the account later does not erase an earlier balance trigger.','S14','Who must file; when to file',value='>USD10,000 aggregate at any time')
row('T08','taxes','Form 8938 — U.S.-living unmarried / separate','Specified foreign financial assets threshold; amounts must exceed either test. Filing conditions and exceptions remain governed by form instructions.','S15','Reporting threshold row',value='>USD50,000 year-end OR >USD75,000 any time')
row('T09','taxes','Form 8938 — U.S.-living joint','Separate from FBAR.','S15','Reporting threshold row',value='>USD100,000 year-end OR >USD150,000 any time')
row('T10','taxes','Form 8938 — abroad unmarried / separate','Use only if the applicable living-abroad test is met; current location alone is insufficient.','S15','Reporting threshold row',value='>USD200,000 year-end OR >USD300,000 any time')
row('T11','taxes','Form 8938 — abroad joint','Use only if applicable abroad requirements are met. Form 8938 is attached to the income-tax return; it does not replace FBAR.','S15','Reporting threshold; when to file',value='>USD400,000 year-end OR >USD600,000 any time')
row('T12','taxes','Genuine foreign gift / inheritance','Form 3520 reporting for gifts/bequests over USD100,000 from nonresident alien individuals/foreign estates, aggregating related parties. Corporate gifts, trusts and covered expatriates differ. Do not relabel existing personal savings as a gift.','S16','Reporting requirements; covered expatriates',value='>USD100,000 for specified individual/estate gifts')
row('T13','taxes','U.S. physical currency reporting','FinCEN 105 requirement applies to more than USD10,000 currency/monetary instruments crossing U.S. border at one time, including family/group aggregation. Not a universal bank-wire tax threshold.','S22','Who must file',value='>USD10,000 total physical currency/instruments')
row('T14','taxes','Streamlined foreign offshore relief','Only qualifying non-willful taxpayers meeting special nonresidency and other eligibility rules. Three covered return years and six FBAR years; pay tax/interest; specified penalties not imposed if requirements satisfied.','S19 S20','Eligibility; scope and effect',pros='Possible lawful penalty relief for qualifying past failures.',cons='Not blanket amnesty; prior penalties not automatically abated; willfulness needs legal review.')
row('T15','taxes','Streamlined domestic offshore procedure','For qualifying non-willful filers meeting prior-return and other criteria: three amended-return years, six FBAR years, tax/interest and defined 5% miscellaneous offshore penalty.','S19 S21','Eligibility; scope and effect',value='5% of defined highest aggregate covered asset balance/value',cons='Not 5% of a wire, not automatic for all U.S. residents, and not a conversion charge.')
row('T16','taxes','Currency gain personal exception — limited reference','The 2024 statutory text includes an exception for a personal disposition of nonfunctional currency if exchange-rate gain does not exceed USD200. It is not USD200 of every gain exempted, not an annual allowance and not a general exclusion for investment transactions.','S18','988(e)',status='Needs review',value='USD200 per qualifying personal transaction in cited edition',cons='Later-amendment status and personal applicability unverified; do not plan splitting to manufacture exemption.')
row('T17','taxes','Treaty, state tax and third-country exposure','IRS treaty index is available for manual review; no treaty rate or exemption applied. User domicile/residence history and state/third-country tax exposure are unknown, so amounts and personalized conclusions remain blank.','S24 S11','Treaty index; worldwide-income rule',status='Unverified',cons='A U.S. passport does not establish every applicable tax jurisdiction; full treaty and local analysis is outside the verified findings.')
